!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = spinal cord
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: Wild type
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = rna sample type: flow through
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = condition: Spinal cord injury
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: spinal cord
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = HA and FT samples underwent on-column DNA digestion using the RNase-Free Dnase Set (Qiagen) and RNA purified with the RNeasy Micro kit (Qiagen). Integrity of the eluted RNA was analyzed by a 2100 Bioanalyzer (Agilent) using the RNA Pico chip. RNA concentration determined by RiboGreen RNA Assay kit (Life Technologies).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = cDNA was generated from 5ng of IP or FT RNA using the Nugen Ovation® 2 RNA-Seq Sytstem V2 kit (Nugen). 1 ug of cDNA was fragmented using the Covaris M220. Paired-end libraries for multiplex sequencing were generated from 300 ng of fragmented cDNA using the Apollo 324 automated library preparation system (Wafergen Biosystems), enriched over 10 cycles of PCR cycles and purified with Agencourt AMPure XP beads (Beckman Coulter).
!Sample_data_processing = Basecalls/demultiplexing performed using Illumina CASAVA 1.8.2
!Sample_data_processing = Aligned to mm10 using STAR2.4.0
!Sample_data_processing = Count read using HT-seq0.6.1 using mm10 RefSeq as reference
!Sample_data_processing = Remove outliers (9595, 791 & 814)
!Sample_data_processing = Normalization (TMM), quantitation (FPKM and adjFPKM) and differential expression analysis using EdgeR. For IP vs IP IP and Flow vs Flow, IP and flow samples were separately analyzed. All samples were included in normalization for IP vs Flow.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
